{
  "id": "80898",
  "type": "Page",
  "tags": [],
  "title": "Common Ion Effect",
  "content": {
    "bibrefs": [],
    "model": [
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "As we learned when we discussed buffer solutions, the hydronium ion concentration in an aqueous solution of acetic acid decreases when the strong electrolyte sodium acetate, NaCH"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "3"
              },
              {
                "text": "CO"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": ", is added. We can explain this effect using Le Châtelier’s principle. The addition of acetate ions causes the equilibrium to shift to the left, decreasing the concentration of H"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "3"
              },
              {
                "text": "O"
              },
              {
                "sup": true,
                "text": "+"
              },
              {
                "text": " to compensate for the increased acetate ion concentration. This increases the concentration of CH"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "3"
              },
              {
                "text": "CO"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": "H:"
              }
            ],
            "id": "1ez9e8f4wdu5ce8",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "0cljjhwfx3qpu2z",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "ajnebhtb9ommyxa",
            "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
            "src": "{\\mathrm{CH}}_3{\\mathrm{CO}}_2\\mathrm H\\;+\\;{\\mathrm H}_2\\mathrm O\\;\\;\\rightleftharpoons\\;\\;{\\mathrm H}_3\\mathrm O^+\\;+\\;{\\mathrm{CH}}_3{\\mathrm{CO}}_2^-",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Because sodium acetate and acetic acid have the acetate ion in common, the influence on the equilibrium is called the "
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "common ion effect"
                  }
                ],
                "content": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "The effect on an existing equilibrium when a substance containing an ion in common with the dissolved species is added to the solution; causes a decrease in the solubility of an ionic species or a decrease in the ionization of a weak acid or base."
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "2689392793",
                    "type": "p"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "1105804365",
                "trigger": "hover",
                "type": "popup"
              },
              {
                "text": "."
              }
            ],
            "id": "h4thy7pxbsi6fjc",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "The common ion effect can also apply to solubility equilibria. Let's look again at the reaction for silver iodide dissolving: "
              }
            ],
            "id": "wy9nds0naeuh42z",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "uxjec3kcjdfiegj",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "3hkhn5k2tz1dc8j",
            "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
            "src": "\\mathrm{AgI}(s)\\;\\;\\rightleftharpoons\\;\\;\\mathrm{Ag}^+(aq)\\;+\\;\\mathrm I^-(aq)",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "If we add potassium iodide (KI) to this solution, we are adding a substance that shares a common ion with silver iodide. Le Châtelier’s principle tells us that when a change is made to a system at equilibrium, the reaction will shift to counteract that change. In this example, there would be an excess of iodide ions, so the reaction would shift toward the left, causing more silver iodide to "
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "precipitate"
                  }
                ],
                "content": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "To cause a substance to separate from a solution as a solid."
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "4173132099",
                    "type": "p"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "4173485614",
                "trigger": "hover",
                "type": "popup"
              },
              {
                "text": " out of solution."
              }
            ],
            "id": "scb6jb4fa0ndy0k",
            "type": "p"
          }
        ],
        "id": "1680465519",
        "selection": {
          "anchor": {
            "offset": 0,
            "path": [
              0,
              0
            ]
          },
          "focus": {
            "offset": 0,
            "path": [
              1,
              0
            ]
          }
        },
        "type": "content"
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Calculate the molar solubility of cadmium sulfide (CdS) in a 0.010-M solution of cadmium bromide (CdBr"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "). The "
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "K"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "sp"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " of CdS is 1.0 × 10"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "–28"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "747k85c52hw6nc3",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "The first thing you should notice is that the cadmium sulfide is dissolved in a solution that contains cadmium ions. We use an ICE table to set up this problem and include the CdBr"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " concentration as a contributor of cadmium ions:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "xcrg29hz4ubd79b",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "___selfClosing___": true,
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "id": "yep527w4cwujtlw",
                            "text": " ",
                            "type": "text"
                          }
                        ],
                        "id": "rf0l3yr3j3fhlnw",
                        "type": "td"
                      },
                      {
                        "align": "center",
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "id": "w1c05yw3zca1my6",
                            "strong": true,
                            "text": "CdS("
                          },
                          {
                            "em": true,
                            "id": "vfi86rc00lc8n3p",
                            "strong": true,
                            "text": "s"
                          },
                          {
                            "id": "eg3cpzahfn8fghr",
                            "strong": true,
                            "text": ") ⇌ Cd"
                          },
                          {
                            "id": "c5q3ekjuhd1xh35",
                            "strong": true,
                            "sup": true,
                            "text": "2+"
                          },
                          {
                            "id": "8ihd9ytfbmzu58z",
                            "strong": true,
                            "text": "("
                          },
                          {
                            "em": true,
                            "id": "0a6r8qlew602cab",
